Objective:
The objective of this project is to implement a binary tree in C++ and efficiently count the leaf nodes and non-leaf nodes present in it.
It aims to demonstrate how each node is checked for the presence of left and right children
to enable accurate counting using traversal.
The project also strengthens understanding of tree creation, insertion,
traversal, and recursion, while handling edge cases
where the tree is empty or contains only a single node.
